# Line-ending policy for a repo edited on Linux and macOS (the two claimed
# CI platforms) and checked out by contributors on any OS.
#
# * text=auto  normalizes CRLF to LF in the repository while keeping native
#              line endings on checkout; combined with eol=lf below, the
#              shell scripts and the extensionless pre-commit hook always
#              stay LF, because a CRLF `#!/bin/sh` shebang is an immediate
#              `bad interpreter` failure.
# *.wasm binary keeps the committed AssemblyScript guests byte-identical to
#              a rebuild: a newline-normalization pass would silently corrupt
#              the artifacts tools/ts/verify.sh diffs against.
* text=auto

# Every file reached through its own shebang is pinned LF, not just the shell
# ones. scripts/sbom.py and scripts/imp-autorecover-loop/loop.py carry
# `#!/usr/bin/env python3` and are run that way (the latter is exec'd by
# run.sh and documented as `./loop.py`), and a CRLF line makes the kernel hand
# the interpreter the name `python3\r`: `env: 'python3\r': No such file or
# directory`. The `*.sh` rule below was written for the shell half of this and
# never covered the Python half.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

*.wasm binary
